# Resolution review

The candidate carries `prior_reviews`: source-reading reviews that left
publication unsettled. Resolve their exact disagreement or stated uncertainty;
do not perform another blind review.

1. Check every material prior claim against source, especially a named disproof
   and any alternate trigger path offered to answer it.
2. Review the report as written. A different trigger, prior state, deployment,
   or consequence may justify a revised report, but cannot rescue this one.
3. Emit Promote or Reject only when the source anchors establish which prior
   reading is correct. Otherwise emit Uncertain and name the remaining fact.

The normal two-Reject safety rule still applies outside this review: your lone
Reject cannot quarantine a finding unless another anchored Reject supports it.
